==Strategy==
After 15 minutes, an Assassin Bear will spawn. They will respawn an infinite amount of times after 2 minutes and 13.33 seconds each time. However, these can easily be defeated by the [[Cat Cannon]].

It is highly recommended you attempt this stage with the original nine [[:Category:Normal Cats|Normal Cats]]' [[True Form]]s. Even then it may be exceedingly difficult, and if having trouble at that point, you should wait to get [[Crazed Cats (origin)|Crazed Cats]] (recommended choices are at least [[Crazed Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Cat]], [[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Tank]], [[Crazed Gross Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Gross]] and [[Crazed Lizard Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Dragon]]) which will make the stage more manageable. Cats with high range like [[Gross Cat (Normal Cat)|Macho Leg]], [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Paris]] and [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|Dragon]] can help a lot, while generally strong or specifically [[:Category:Anti-Traitless Cats|anti-Traitless]] [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber Rares]] can make a huge difference. Having at least one powerful [[:Category:Anti-Red Cats|anti-Red Cat]] is also very important. Compared to its nail-biting predecessor, [[Pitfall Zone]], this stage is relatively straightforward. Remember the [[Ururun Wolf (Special Cat)|Ururun Wolf]] drop is not guaranteed so make sure to use a Treasure Radar (or just use a Gold CPU + a treasure radar)

